Chapter: CrossUnsupportedProbe

 A file read on a target that has no filesystem. `read-file-raw` is a real
 builtin and reaches the plug builtin table, so the arm64 and riscv plugs
 must refuse to emit for it rather than answering the empty string.

 The subject of `build/cross-unsupported-test.ps1`. It carries a `.skip`
 because the default battery is x86-64, where this program is ordinary and
 proves nothing.

  opening : [Console, FileSystem] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni ("got:" & read-file-raw "NOTE.TXT")
  end
